# A POSIX shell will not run a script with CRLF line endings: the shebang comes
# out as `bash\r`, and the error names that rather than the script, so it reads
# as a missing interpreter instead of a mangled file.
#
# This rule was `build-aux/android/*.sh`, which was too narrow. The Android
# build runs Meson against this Windows checkout, and
# `build-aux/compile-blueprints.sh` — which every platform's build calls — came
# out with CRLF and stopped the build 2654 targets in. None of these are ever
# run by a Windows shell, so all of them can simply be LF.
*.sh text eol=lf
